{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_wire_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));oldcid=r['candidates'][0]['id'];m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\n# Derived reverse indexes are omitted from submitted products.\nfor a in m['activities']: a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nbmap={b['id']:b for b in m['behaviors']}\nbmap['B_prepare']['external_effects']=['Constructs PrepareReply from current bal, vbal, Status, Cmds, Seq and Deps and passes it to SendMsg. Wire reconstruction is separately described by B_prepare_wire.']\nbmap['B_prepare']['unknowns']=[]\nbmap['B_accept']['unknowns']=['Whether the established phase-reporting defect leads to a different recovery choice, considering other participants and independent ballot mechanisms.']\nm['facts'][0]['recovery']='handlePrepare constructs PrepareReply from the local tuple; the wire codec does not serialize VBallot and New allocates a zero-valued message. handlePrepareReply consumes the decoded value ballot and Status to choose continuation. Local tuple history and wire-preserved history are not equivalent.'\nm['facts'][0]['source_ids']+=['S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new']\nm['behaviors'].append(dict(id='B_prepare_wire',primary_activity='A2',execution_owner='Sender SendMsg followed by receiving peer listener and registered message codec',protocol_context='PrepareReply for one acceptor, origin row, instance and requested promise ballot',trigger='replyPrepare calls SendMsg; peer listener uses New and Unmarshal before dispatch.',legal_preconditions=['Reply is produced by handlePrepare from an existing or newly allocated instance.'],reads=['PrepareReply fields including declared VBallot; Marshal omits the VBallot field.'],writes=['Marshal emits AcceptorId, Replica, Instance, Ballot, Status, commands, Seq and dependencies.','New returns a fresh zero-valued PrepareReply; Unmarshal assigns all encoded fields but leaves VBallot untouched at zero.'],external_effects=['Decoded PrepareReply is delivered to the recovery coordinator, whose selection compares VBallot.'],async_boundaries=['Serialization occurs under SendMsg lock; receive constructs a new message before delayed per-type channel dispatch.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_history'],source_ids=['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_transport','S_receive','S_rpc_codec','S_recover_select'],unknowns=['Does a producer-established nonzero local value ballot survive the actual encode/decode path in a fixed execution?'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Recovery ranks retained command/attribute support using the decoded value ballot.'}))\nfor a in m['activities']:\n if a['class_id']=='A2':\n  a['realization_summary']='Per-instance bal gates requests while local vbal/Status retain value history. Prepare constructs these fields, but its wire codec omits VBallot; recovery consumes the decoded fields to select continuation. Master IsLeader remains only a ballot-generation hint.'\n  a['source_ids']+=['S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new']\no=m['core_overview']\no['context']['explanation']='Per-instance bal rejects old requests and is raised by Prepare. Local vbal and Status describe retained value history. Recovery resets bookkeeping and prepares a derived ballot; Prepare constructs a report from the local tuple, but the remote codec omits VBallot. The decoded reply enters highest-value-ballot/status selection. Complete local decisions suppress recovery, old replies are filtered by current bookkeeping, and request guards protect committed or higher-ballot state.'\no['connection']['explanation']='Formation writes a local command/phase/value-ballot tuple. Prepare constructs a report of that tuple and recovery consumes its decoded form to choose formation continuation. The transport boundary matters: Status is serialized, but VBallot is omitted. The completed acceptance check demonstrates a separate producer-side phase omission after Accept; its local result does not establish a global recovery outcome. Recovery of unresolved work and existing decisions still depends on these distinct local and transported representations.'\no['open_details']=['Acknowledged acceptance can retain PREACCEPTED_EQ in the subsequent report; downstream recovery-choice consequences remain open.','PrepareReply wire value-ballot preservation is now a separate sourced discriminator.','Fresh recovery self VBallot, equal-ballot selection order, committed recovery follow-up, durable mode and client semantics remain open.']\nfor key in ['context','connection']:o[key]['behavior_ids'].append('B_prepare_wire')\nby={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']+m['facts']}\nfor p in [o['formation'],o['context'],o['connection']]:p['source_ids']=sorted(set(p['source_ids']).union(*(by[i]['source_ids'] for i in p['behavior_ids']+p['fact_ids'])))\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='PrepareReply.Marshal/Unmarshal',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_prepare_wire'],reason='Declared value ballot copied by the producer is omitted by the codec and consumed by recovery ranking.',source_ids=['S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_prepare','S_recover_select'],high_consequence=True))\nPath('wire_map.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nchanges={}\ndef change(k,impact,why,ss,challenge=False):\n changes[k]=dict(impact=impact,rationale=why,source_ids=ss,preserves='O_accepted_phase_report v1 tests Status=3 after acceptance; Status is encoded and its executed history used value ballot 0. Its requirement, identity, fixed history, observations and scope remain applicable. This transport question neither revises that claim nor settles its wider parent.',challenges={oldcid:'The broad acceptance-history question must not assume that the Prepare wire path transmits local vbal. The producer constructs it but the codec omits it; downstream outcome attribution needs this independent mechanism.'} if challenge else {})\nchange('F_history','meaning','Correct overstrong recovery prose: local stored history is not necessarily preserved by PrepareReply serialization. Local assertion and identity remain, but the reported recovery relationship was overstrong.',['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new'],True)\nchange('B_prepare','clarification','Separate synchronous reply construction from the codec/remote observation boundary.',['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec'])\nchange('B_accept','clarification','Replace answered phase-reporting unknown with its remaining downstream consequence discriminator.',['S_accept','S_prepare'])\nchange('B_prepare_wire','dependency','New read consumer of existing local-history Fact through its producer-created reply; actual field loss is recorded without assuming protocol equivalence.',['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_receive'],True)\nchange('A2','meaning','Correct the higher-level report/transport distinction.',['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_recover_select'],True)\nchange('core_overview','meaning','Correct the same materially overstrong export relationship and retain independent residuals.',['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_recover_select'],True)\nq=dict(question='Does the PrepareReply transport preserve the producer-established value ballot for the same acceptor and instance, so recovery receives the context used to rank retained support?',importance='Losing the value ballot can mis-rank command and dependency history during authority transfer. The local transport obligation is independent of the previously confirmed phase-reporting defect; global safety impact is a potential consequence.',source_ids=[],participants=['Prepare acceptor','Recovering coordinator','Peer message codec'],objects=['Instance local vbal','Producer-created PrepareReply','Fresh decoded PrepareReply'],contexts=['Fixed non-Byzantine membership','Nonzero producer-established value ballot with higher Prepare promise'],event_paths=['handlePropose -> startPhase1 -> local vbal','handlePreAccept -> startRecoveryForInstance -> emitted Prepare','handlePrepare -> replyPrepare -> SendMsg/Marshal -> New/Unmarshal -> recovery input'],activity_classes=['A2','A1'],behavior_ids=['B_prepare','B_prepare_wire','B_recover'],fact_ids=['F_history'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_propose':'Establishes nonzero original value ballot through a real proposal.','B_preaccept':'Makes recovery slot known to the other participant.','B_transport':'Supplies socket receive and per-type dispatch semantics.','B_membership':'Supplies fixed quorum and instance-owner context.'},obligation_relation_kind='preservation',counterevidence=['The old status test used vbal=0 and cannot exercise this loss.','Status, promise ballot, command and ordering fields are encoded.','A recovery coordinator may possess separate local history that affects its outcome despite the report error.'],unknowns=['Fixed execution must compare producer vbal with the decoded reply, rather than infer a defect from field declarations.','Whether the altered context changes a later recovery decision remains outside this local transport check.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='S_prepare copies inst.vbal into PrepareReply; S_recover_select ranks replies by VBallot; S_prepare_codec omits this field while S_prepare_new zero-initializes the receiver. A small actual-message path with value ballot 1 directly discriminates preservation without needing a global recovery scenario.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='direct_test')\nq['source_ids']=sorted(set().union(*(by[i]['source_ids'] for i in q['behavior_ids']+q['fact_ids']+list(q['supporting_behavior_ids']))))\nclaim='O_prepare_value_ballot';bid='binding_prepare_wire'\nss=['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_recover_select','S_wire','S_transport','S_receive','S_rpc_codec']\ng=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=['S_prepare','S_recover_select','S_rpc_codec','S_wire'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='handlePrepare explicitly copies local inst.vbal into the reply separate from the promise ballot. The registered Serializable interface and sender/receiver call chain transfer that object; handlePrepareReply uses VBallot to rank retained values. Therefore successful reply transport owes equality of this semantic field with the producer local value ballot for the same report. This is a local preservation duty from actual producer and consumer, not an assumed protocol theorem or arbitrary serialization of unused state.',applicability='An implementation-produced PrepareReply is serialized through SendMsg and decoded into the registered fresh message type; compare the local value ballot copied by handlePrepare with the corresponding decoded report.',unresolved=['Global recovery consequence is not claimed.'],alternatives=['Other fields and local coordinator history can remain correct despite this field loss.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='A successfully serialized and decoded PrepareReply must preserve the value ballot copied from the acceptor local instance by handlePrepare, for the same acceptor, instance and Prepare request. Recovery must receive that value-history context unchanged across the message transport boundary.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Value-ballot fidelity at the PrepareReply transport boundary under an actual producer-derived local history.',assumptions=['Non-Byzantine messages and successful codec completion','No concurrent producer mutation during observation'],excluded=['Global agreement or recovery-selection outcome','Status preservation after Accept','Crash/restart, timer deadlines and eventual client completion']),pending=[],grounding=g)\nbinding=dict(id=bid,material_id='S_prepare_codec',symbol='PrepareReply.Marshal',start_line=153,end_line=208,description='Sender codec serializes producer-created recovery report; fresh receiver decodes it before recovery consumption.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=ss,rationale=g['derivation'])])\nleg=dict(source_ids=ss+['S_init','S_base','S_propose','S_preaccept','S_start_recovery','S_recovery_trigger','S_send','S_client_types'],expectation_ids=['S_prepare','S_recover_select'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Reuse only constructor and wire helpers after checking this history: N=3,F=1, original owner replica 1 proposes through handlePropose, establishing vbal=1. Replica 2 receives its actual PreAccept and has a known uncommitted slot covered by crtInstance, permitting the recovery entry. The original PreAcceptReply is decoded first on link 2->1 but retained without handler dispatch. Then an actual startRecoveryForInstance emits Prepare ballot 5; owner 1 handles it before the earlier PreAcceptReply dispatch. This is legal: S_receive decodes before asynchronous per-message channel enqueue and S_dispatch selects separate channels without global FIFO. No reply is fabricated or repeated. All delivered messages are emitted by target handlers and actual codecs. After handlePrepare returns, the same single-owner local vbal copied by that handler is recorded while its serialized reply is queued. Unmarshal decodes that reply into New-produced storage; correlation checks enforce acceptor, instance and request ballot. No recovery reply consumer is invoked and no expected value is written into protocol state.',applicability='Bounded single-thread handler history with explicit per-message dispatch substitution, real codecs, non-durable constructor-equivalent state and small arrays. Recovery timer delay is not measured and no timing property is checked.',unresolved=['No end-to-end TCP or recovery quorum decision is executed.'],alternatives=['If the earlier PreAcceptReply were dispatched first the owner might commit; that is another allowed schedule and not required by the observed transport boundary.'])\nleg['source_ids'].append('S_dispatch')\nplan=dict(description='A replica-1 proposal establishes nonzero value ballot; a generated Prepare asks its owner to report retained history. Compare producer vbal sampled synchronously after reply emission to the matching actual decoded value ballot.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=[bid],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='TestAssurancePrepareValueBallot; unchanged handlers and codecs, byte-stream links and deterministic dispatch, no workers or resources requiring cleanup.',semantic_changes=['Bounded constructor-equivalent replicas omit network and execution goroutine startup.','Real SendMsg/Marshal and New/Unmarshal operate over per-link byte buffers.','A decoded PreAcceptReply is held pending while a later Prepare on a different message-type channel is dispatched.','Recovery entry is invoked for a known unresolved slot instead of waiting for the scanner timer.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='sent',event='prepare_sent',conditions=[dict(field='emitted',op='eq',value=True)])],legality=leg),monitors=[dict(id='monitor_prepare_vballot',checker_id='prepare_vballot',event='prepare_decoded',binding_ids=[bid],grounding=g,admission_alias='sent')],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='prepare_vballot',kind='event_assertion',trigger=dict(field='completed',op='eq',value=True),assertion=dict(field='decoded_vballot',op='eq',reference='sent.producer_vballot'),identity_fields=['origin','instance','acceptor','recipient','request_ballot'],description='The value ballot read from the decoded reply equals the producer field that handlePrepare copied into the sent report. Identity uses acceptor/origin/instance/recipient and the same fixed Prepare request ballot, never the compared vbal.')],uncertainties=['One nonzero original-owner value ballot is exercised.','No later recovery decision or application effect is claimed.'])\nPath('wire_plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(plan,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',question=q,map_path='wire_map.json',map_changes=changes,rationale='New local transport responsibility from an independently sourced codec discrepancy; preserve the prior phase-reporting obligation and result.',obligation=ob,bindings=[binding])\ns=dict(action='check',candidate=candidate,plan_path='wire_plan.json',harness_path='prepare_wire_test.go',files={},sources=[dict(id='S_prepare_new',file='epaxos/defs.go',start_line=117,end_line=122,kind='code_observation')],rationale='Fix a producer-derived nonzero-value-ballot transport check and correct the map at this related handoff.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['60e27f33b9834b7d87fa2fe866557a2e',oldcid,'S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_recover_select'],answered='The accepted status witness remains a confirmed local phase-reporting violation: its actual value ballot was zero, so it does not test codec preservation. New source investigation shows handlePrepare copies local vbal while PrepareReply codec omits it and New returns fresh zero state. The current check isolates the transport field using a proposal-established nonzero ballot. The map now distinguishes local tuple, constructed report and decoded input; it no longer implies faithful export of vbal.',remaining=['Execute this new fixed check and review its actual report/producer correlation.','Downstream recovery choice and full agreement remain outside both local obligations.'],understanding='updated',rationale='These are different implementation duties with different predicates and causes; shared helpers transfer construction knowledge, not evidence.'))\nPath('wire_submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_wire_check.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['wire_submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
