=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=ss,rationale=g['derivation'])])\nleg=dict(source_ids=ss+['S_init','S_base','S_propose','S_preaccept','S_start_recovery','S_recovery_trigger','S_send','S_client_types'],expectation_ids=['S_prepare','S_recover_select'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Reuse only constructor and wire helpers after checking this history: N=3,F=1, original owner replica 1 proposes through handlePropose, establishing vbal=1. Replica 2 receives its actual PreAccept and has a known uncommitted slot covered by crtInstance, permitting the recovery entry. The original PreAcceptReply is decoded first on link 2->1 but retained without handler dispatch. Then an actual startRecoveryForInstance emits Prepare ballot 5; owner 1 handles it before the earlier PreAcceptReply dispatch. This is legal: S_receive decodes before asynchronous per-message channel enqueue and S_dispatch selects separate channels without global FIFO. No reply is fabricated or repeated. All delivered messages are emitted by target handlers and actual codecs. After handlePrepare returns, the same single-owner local vbal copied by that handler is recorded while its serialized reply is queued. Unmarshal decodes that reply into New-produced storage; correlation checks enforce acceptor, instance and request ballot. No recovery reply consumer is invoked and no expected value is written into protocol state.',applicability='Bounded single-thread handler history with explicit per-message dispatch substitution, real codecs, non-durable constructor-equivalent state and small arrays. Recovery timer delay is not measured and no timing property is checked.',unresolved=['No end-to-end TCP or recovery quorum decision is executed.'],alternatives=['If the earlier PreAcceptReply were dispatched first the owner might commit; that is another allowed schedule and not required by the observed transport boundary.'])\nleg['source_ids'].append('S_dispatch')\nplan=dict(description='A replica-1 proposal establis